        {
          "id": 526529199,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The lowest level routine (`byte_to_hex`) does a post-increment  (`*out++ =`) on the pointer.  \n`word_to_hex` and `dword_to_hex` were the examples I followed.  \n  \nI thought about making another routine for completeness but it didn't seem that the similar `guint8_to_hex` is used very much.  \nAt that point I was trying to minimize the number of files in the patch (1 vs 3). But that was before the merge request ran the pipeline and failed on the tests. %-)  No problem making a `guint24_to_hex` if that is best solution.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
